<title>USA: ImClone cancer drug results &quot;promising&quot;.</title>
<headline>ImClone cancer drug results &quot;promising&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>ImClone Systems Inc said Monday that results of a preclinical study of its lead cancer therapeutic, C225, an epidermal growth factor receptor antagonist, were &quot;promising.&quot;</p>
<p>ImClone said that treatment with C225 in human bladder carcinoma cells growing orthotopically in mice resulted in a significant inhibition of tumor growth compared with controls.</p>
<p>The company said that the orthotopic approach utilized in this study is a cancer model that implants human tumor cells into the tissue of origin in the mouse, thus making the model a more realistic indicator of tumor progression.</p>
</text>
